{"id": "EUVD-2026-76434", "enisaUuid": "558a53e2-b88e-36db-bb7f-355dc5b01509", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsvcrdma: Reject Read lists that exceed the page budget\n\nIndividual Read segment lengths are validated at decode time, but\nnothing prevents a requester from sending multiple segments whose\ncumulative length exceeds the rq_pages array budget. When one\nsegment fills the page array exactly, the runtime guard in\nsvc_rdma_build_read_segment() is bypassed because len reaches zero.\nA subsequent segment then accesses the NULL sentinel slot at\nrq_pages[rq_maxpages], resulting in a NULL pointer dereference during\nDMA mapping.\n\nAccumulate pages across all Read segments and reject the message at\ndecode time when the total would overflow the page budget.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:41", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/beb4e9801f6362436102acc4cc5304b7324f9365", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e70fdb121171c3eb0ac34eb545721828cd737717", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a3af2262cb384112ef38632de4690682be528b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/465f511f59a0fa7a80d5d1073c4b24f28ea38f58", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ca487abb3bdf581851664b5db21f364caf57682"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89528", "GHSA-4rjj-pgm8-m2r9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "348ae5b0-fda3-3236-9fd3-b63f62c87697", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "53cec62a-eb07-38ea-b000-6bdd150a1fd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "026d958b38c628a1b4ced534808945365e2747a5 <465f511f59a0fa7a80d5d1073c4b24f28ea38f58"}, {"id": "5bac1104-b43d-341b-8999-07f4d64c17a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p